<item><title>Niger records 7,116 road accidents in 2025, with 1,245 killed</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-records-7-116-road-accidents-in-2025-with-1-245-killed-51678d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-records-7-116-road-accidents-in-2025-with-1-245-killed-51678d/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>Transport Minister Colonel Major Abdourahamane Amadou announced the figures ahead of the 15th African Road Safety Day, and the government has declared 2026 the year of road.</description><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:43:37 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-records-7-116-road-accidents-in-2025-with-1-245-killed-51678d/share.jpg" length="39932" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-records-7-116-road-accidents-in-2025-with-1-245-killed-51678d/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Niger&apos;s security forces kill five mercenaries and seize weapons in first half of November</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-s-security-forces-kill-five-mercenaries-and-seize-b8a377/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-s-security-forces-kill-five-mercenaries-and-seize-b8a377/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>The Centre Intégré de Coordination des Opérations says the operations ran from 1 to 12 November and recovered a cache of rocket launchers in the east.</description><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:18:54 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" length="31036" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
